{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1078 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "ef4df7aade4119f55efee0bdc206ebe32ff983f5c1db45e79dc20cca55fe6ce5" :edb/db-before-t 1077 :edb/db-after-t 1078 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534390 50 #inst "2026-10-06T23:42:07.205Z" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110216 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/bdb5279236cdc7671efa0f309b0a07d5ffc131f9d3c33a048f286fdef4588fcd.png)\n\nWhich system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110216 1100 "Which system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/3edbb889f6978133fc2ae041a3085a33.png)" 13194139534390 false] [17592186110216 1145 "Consider the line $y = 2x - 1$. Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq 2x - 1\n$$\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = -x+2\n$$\n\nSince the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq -x + 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y \\le 2x - 1; y \\ge - x + 2\n$$" 13194139534390 false] [17592186110216 1145 "Consider the line $y = 2x - 1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq 2x - 1.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y = -x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq -x + 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x-1 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110461 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/c9209c8978b86043b5d57d4a357a480a0209914598a0d7f2a810539cc050c473.png)\n\nWhich system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110461 1100 "Which system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/344928c0eea99cd3497661d8845d95b4.png)" 13194139534390 false] [17592186110461 1145 "Consider the line $y=2x-3$. Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\gt 2x - 3$.\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = x + 1\n$$\n\nSince the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\lt x+1$.\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n${y > 2x - 3; y < x + 1$." 13194139534390 false] [17592186110461 1145 "Consider the line $y=2x-3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\gt 2x - 3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y = x + 1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\lt x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y<x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110462 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/69a4b7d160f9a3990034f7e9170cc20d90eba33bd87397f8436836fdd5520e84.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110462 1100 "Which of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/457d1898a5945703bd6b2621ffa8f08a.png)" 13194139534390 false] [17592186110462 1145 "Consider the line\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3\n$$\n\nSince the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3\n$$\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = x+2\n$$\n\nSince the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\lt x+2$.\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y \\le \\frac{1}{3}x + 3; y < x + 2\n$$" 13194139534390 false] [17592186110462 1145 "Consider the line $y = \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y = x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\lt x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{3}x+3 \\\\ y<x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110463 1100 "What system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e92ea6fc292a771333cc12b9554b58bd4ba5f358195982c5ac3fd6bd2a9d06ff.png)" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110463 1100 "What system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/8d691714edd32c1331cb1041545ed34e.png)" 13194139534390 false] [17592186110463 1145 "Consider the line $y=1$. Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y < 1$.\n\nNow consider the line $x - y = 2$. Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n$y =x- 2$.\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq x - 2\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-y \\leq 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y < 1; x - y \\le 2\n$$" 13194139534390 false] [17592186110463 1145 "Consider the line $y=1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is \n\n$$\ny < 1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $x - y = 2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny =x- 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq  x - 2,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-y \\leq 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<1 \\\\ x-y\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186110577 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285664 13194139534390 true] [17592186110577 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285699 13194139534390 true] [17592186110577 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285727 13194139534390 true] [17592186110577 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285734 13194139534390 true] [17592186110577 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285769 13194139534390 true] [17592186110578 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285692 13194139534390 true] [17592186110578 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285706 13194139534390 true] [17592186110578 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285713 13194139534390 true] [17592186110578 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285776 13194139534390 true] [17592186110578 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285783 13194139534390 true] [17592186110579 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285671 13194139534390 true] [17592186110579 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285678 13194139534390 true] [17592186110579 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285741 13194139534390 true] [17592186110579 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285748 13194139534390 true] [17592186110584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285657 13194139534390 true] [17592186110584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285685 13194139534390 true] [17592186110584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285720 13194139534390 true] [17592186110584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285755 13194139534390 true] [17592186110584 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285762 13194139534390 true] [17592186111346 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534390 true] [17592186111346 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/06519bbe714e1ad2e8b878e7c6a6026cbad7b846b06f16fbdd3c478c18f9db88.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139534390 true] [17592186111346 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/q-90171.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139534390 false] [17592186111346 1145 "Consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $x-4y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{4}+2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{x}{4}+2,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-4y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x \\\\ x-4y\\ge -8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285658 13194139534390 true] [17592186285657 1089 "q-109971" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285657 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534390 true] [17592186285657 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/301b3a5f659be1efaa44d359d36acb055d45181b4d4e27b63f9fba7136e34867.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285657 1113 #uuid "72b9639e-3c97-59a1-8d1b-9bc526399985" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285657 1145 "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"gretaer than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285659 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285660 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285661 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285662 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285663 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1041 "selection" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285659 13194139534390 true] [17592186285658 1110 #uuid "75867289-1a78-56c2-87a9-0e701061722a" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285659 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285659 1111 #uuid "72443398-a4be-5ae0-95b9-bcb3fa2f8c88" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285660 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285660 1111 #uuid "21b59f67-c132-5893-a261-928896093713" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285661 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\le -2\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285661 1111 #uuid "b1493575-3968-5c23-b3dc-de5e20d424f2" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285662 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y<\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y>-2\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285662 1111 #uuid "34684f91-5ec5-5189-a631-41707dc1b4fc" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285663 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\le -2\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285663 1111 #uuid "9333e418-2366-5278-97