\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x-4,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285673 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285674 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285675 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285676 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285677 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1041 "selection" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285677 13194139534390 true] [17592186285672 1110 #uuid "c6d5d5a9-4693-5ade-aa80-35bfbbeb6fea" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285673 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le -8 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285673 1111 #uuid "2e20c320-1ad0-54fd-9512-fca352d508eb" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285674 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y>-8 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285674 1111 #uuid "7520387a-23fa-57dd-a52f-8ec8d9a1cbc6" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285675 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285675 1111 #uuid "086537ea-0bb8-55cd-8b01-4ba255c377ac" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285676 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285676 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285676 1111 #uuid "a52f7431-2a01-5a64-9d67-f90694e6a8c0" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285677 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285677 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285677 1111 #uuid "f74537c3-6e60-5002-ad5b-e9e4dd1021fb" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285678 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285679 13194139534390 true] [17592186285678 1089 "q-110093" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285678 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534390 true] [17592186285678 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/f03b04087cde111d9db2b9e499a0d700105b7150496cc6c117c0f2e2b05e74c2.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285678 1113 #uuid "2dff6eda-c649-5ce9-b940-098322fd6bdf" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285678 1145 "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $3x+2y=-6.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{2}x-3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le -\\frac{3}{2}x-3,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n3x+2y\\le -6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\