e $x+2y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+1,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285743 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285744 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285745 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285746 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285747 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1041 "selection" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1104 #edb/ref 17592186285744 13194139534390 true] [17592186285742 1110 #uuid "4f5ba861-bd3f-5bdc-8a99-8037a316c2c9" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285743 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285743 1111 #uuid "66a652be-4ace-51bb-9d9a-d7be8d4af41b" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285744 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534390 true] [17592186285744 1111 #uuid "ac94eeb5-f671-5969-9c0b-4b4255577d9e" 13194139534390 true] [17592186285745 1034 "{\\begin{aligned